{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>At the end of seven years</b> etc. At the beginning of the year, so that they may learn all year, as it proceeds to explain. <b>At the festival of Sukkot</b> — when all Israel comes, etc." "<b>In the year of the release, at the set time.</b> Since it is the first year of the seven-year shemittah cycle, why does it call it <b>the year of the shemittah</b>? Answer: because the law of the seventh year still applies to it regarding the harvest that comes from the harvest of the seventh year."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:51.434480174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}